    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0688" n="667" xml:id="pg667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.811/8–648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in the United Kingdom
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-07T14:00:00-04:00">August 7, 1948—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3130. Brit Emb has not yet recd instructions referred to urtel 3566 Aug 6.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d430-f1"/>
                    However, from your summary it seems to us that Dept position contained Dudel 24, rptd London 3101 and Paris 2999 and
                        Dudel 25, rptd London 3113 and Paris
                        3013,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d430-f2"/> not essentially divergent UK attitude.
                        USDel Belgrade already authorized support
                    Brit resolution on Court ref and we prepared to have USDel further support existence rights under 1921 Convention of UK,
                    France, and other 1921 Convention signatories in final summation US position at
                    Conf. In our concept it is desirable such support be given in conjunction with
                    ref issues of Western Power participation, UN association, Austrian membership,
                    Sov monopolistic control Danube, etc., which we consider more basic and on which
                    we accordingly feel emphasis should be placed.</p>
                <p>In circumstances problem now apparently one of timing. We continue to feel
                    strongly that Cannon’s appraisal importance remaining to end valid. That
                    procedure will enable us extract from Conf maximum public clarification
                    divergence Western-Sov objectives. In addition, and more importantly, we would
                    anticipate undesirable repercussions in other international forums should the
                    Western powers withdraw prematurely from this first Conf wherein we are a
                    minority.</p>
                <p>Sent London 3130 rptd Paris 3023 Belgrade 466 Dudel 28.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
